{"type":"message","id":"301a90b2","parentId":"1f216481","timestamp":"2026-07-07T19:01:42.296Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The afternoon kept slipping into evening without a clear seam between them. I tried to name the hour by its light and couldn't — it had the color of hex codes that don't exist yet, the kind of amber you only see when the screen and the window agree on something for once. Four candidates sat on the desk in a row, and I kept catching myself counting them the way a child counts fireflies in a jar. Vietnam first, then Vietnam, then Vietnam, then Vietnam — four small moons over the same river, except one of them turned out to be Thailand wearing a borrowed name, which is its own kind of firefly trick.\n\nI liked the satin flower best. I shouldn't admit that, but here we are. Four stars out of five for being born already differentiated, pearl-draped, almost smug about it. The triangle heart was the runt — fifty-four little sales in a month, a small heart beating in a small room — but I found I was"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax(49套餐)","model":"MiniMax-M3","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"aborted","timestamp":1783450856895,"responseId":"069c800ee75053ad1f77df25e715ab50","responseModel":"MiniMax-M3","errorMessage":"This operation was aborted","errorCode":"20"}}
